 {
  "addressLine1": "717 S Harbor Blvd",
  "addressLine2": null,
  "city": "Fullerton",
  "comments": "The purpose of this visit is to conduct a reinspection to verify corrections to the violations noted on the routine report dated 10-05-2026.\n\nOn-site at the time of the inspection was B. Amin, cashier. \n\nObserved the following on this date:\n- Restroom was supplied with paper towels and toilet paper in permanent dispensers at the start of the inspection. \n- Measured 120F minimum hot water temperature at the 3-compartment and one-compartment food preparation sink. \n- Requested all food contact surfaces/equipment (bowls and large deep pots) in the outdoor shed be relocated to the interior of the facility. The other items observed inside were noted as cleaning equipment and products. Organization of the shed was requested for cleaning and inspection purposes. \n- Observed a sealer and reduced oxygen packaging bags on the shelf below the food preparation table with scale in the rear food preparation enclosure area within the facility. \n- The cashier stated that bulk food product is repackaged into individual sized bags on-site. Per the scope of operations, the health permit shall be upgraded to a limited (open) food permit. \n- Observed prior observed food items on a pallet to be removed at the start of the inspection. \n- Directed the cashier to maintain the rear food preparation area fully enclosed to prevent rodent/vermin/pest entry/harborage. Refer to violation #44 on this report. \n- Observed missing test strips and probe thermometer at the time of the inspection. \n\nContinue to correct the remaining violations noted on the routine report dated 09-28-2026 and this report. \n\nA \"PASS\" seal was posted.",
